      "fields": {
        "Title": "Zurich Art Salon ",
        "Slug": "zurich-art-salon",
        "Date": "2026-08-06T00:00:00.000Z",
        "Location": "Halle 622 Zurich ",
        "Gallery Rep": "Maison d’Art ",
        "Image": "https://framerusercontent.com/images/xtk7k7Zt2Nt3dhngELYGY9ORagA.png",
        "Curatorial Statement": [
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "id": "v:dXmgRB6uO/U49nfym_y:0",
            "attributes": {
              "tag": "p"
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "TextRun",
                "id": "v:dXmgRB6uO/U49nfym_y:0:0",
                "attributes": {
                  "text": "In 2025, Boky Hackel-Ward exhibited at Art Salon Zürich, a boutique art fair dedicated to modern and contemporary art by post-1945 artists. She was represented at the fair by Maison d'Art (Monte Carlo), which presented her work alongside pieces by Nicolas Guzmán, Marcello Lo Giudice, Carlos Rolón and Pablo Armesto."
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "Image 2": "https://framerusercontent.com/images/wRSb7zKPMLCjZ7l6nkxRKusBGMg.png",
        "Content 1": [
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "id": "v:dXmgRB6uO/hOht0kN8p:0",
            "attributes": {
              "tag": "p"
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "TextRun",
                "id": "v:dXmgRB6uO/hOht0kN8p:0:0",
                "attributes": {
                  "text": "At the heart of the presentation was "
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "TextRun",
                "id": "v:dXmgRB6uO/hOht0kN8p:0:1",
                "attributes": {
                  "text": "Damaged",
                  "italic": true
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "TextRun",
                "id": "v:dXmgRB6uO/hOht0kN8p:0:2",
                "attributes": {
                  "text": ", shown in its gold-leaf edition — edition one of six — from Boky's Figurative Poetry Collection. The work distills the language central to her practice: a fragmented figure whose broken surfaces are gilded rather than concealed, holding beauty and rupture within a single form. Finished in gold leaf, "
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "TextRun",
                "id": "v:dXmgRB6uO/hOht0kN8p:0:3",
                "attributes": {
                  "text": "Damaged",
                  "italic": true
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "TextRun",
                "id": "v:dXmgRB6uO/hOht0kN8p:0:4",
                "attributes": {
                  "text": " transforms absence and injury into something luminous — a quiet meditation on resilience and the poetry of the incomplete."
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "id": "v:dXmgRB6uO/hOht0kN8p:1",
            "attributes": {
              "tag": "p"
            },
            "children": [
